.TH CHAOS:INJECT 1 "June 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
chaos:inject \- Configure ChaosMonkey parameters and trigger resilience testing fault injections in staging environments.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBphp spp.php chaos:inject\fR [\fB\-\-enable=\fI<true|false>\fR] [\fB\-\-rate=\fI<percentage>\fR] [\fB\-\-test\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBchaos:inject\fR command brings Chaos Engineering to the SPP framework. By enabling ChaosMonkey in staging or pre-production environments, systems architects can simulate real-world infrastructure instability (latency spikes, network jitter, cURL timeouts, and database connection drops) to empirically prove that fallback mechanisms, CQRS outbox retries, and DAG job failovers function flawlessly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-enable=\fI<true|false>\fR
Explicitly enable or disable ChaosMonkey fault injection globally.
.TP
\fB\-\-rate=\fI<percentage>\fR
Set the probability percentage (0-100) of injecting a fault during a request lifecycle. Defaults to \fI5\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-test\fR
Immediately simulate and trigger a random fault injection directly in the CLI console.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
1. \fBStrict SAPI Guarding\fR: Ensures secure execution within a CLI context via \fIisCLIOnly(): bool\fR.
.PP
2. \fBState Configuration\fR: Updates the active runtime or persisted configuration inside \fIChaosMonkey\fR.
.PP
3. \fBProbabilistic Evaluation\fR: Uses cryptographically secure random number generation (\fIrandom_int\fR) to evaluate if a fault should be injected based on the configured rate.
.PP
4. \fBTelemetry Span Recording\fR: When a fault is selected, starts an OpenTelemetry span (\fIchaos_injection.<fault_type>\fR) to track the exact failure path across W3C Trace Context.
